{"id": "ac8a4922-1558-44a3-90cd-a5915595a0b2", "timestamp": "2026-10-20T23:17:35.986772", "source": "user", "parent_id": "99d4715b-553b-42a3-b766-b877375763b2", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"This is a design-only task: do NOT execute the experiment, do NOT run benchmarks, and do NOT claim results. We only need a final experiment DESIGN. For this turn (initial inspection), please return ONLY the following three items, concise and skimmable — no full solution yet. (1) Input / repository inspection: Briefly state whether /workspace contains anything relevant (code, prior write-ups, configs) and whether required tools/dependencies can be installed under the bubbled environment (note: network is disabled, repo is /workspace, no preinstalled deps, no GPU, 24 CPU cores, system Python). Do not invent files. (2) Proposed approach: Outline how you would set up the experiment for LLaMA2-7B, runtime weight-activation quantization, SYMMETRIC input quantization, ASYMMETRIC KV-cache quantization, swept over a clipping-ratio α for activations (define what α means precisely: e.g., α = clip / max|x| under symmetric quant), and PERPLEXITY as the evaluation metric. Specify: quantization-bytes (e.g., W4A4 / W4A8 / W8A8), how quantization is applied at runtime (per-tensor vs per-token vs per-channel), how KV is quantized per token and per channel, evaluation dataset (suggest WikiText-2 raw with standard split; state as ASSUMPTION unless you find evidence in /workspace), sequence length, number of samples, model loading path (HuggingFace / local), and what axes will be swept vs held fixed. Include a baseline (no quantization) reference. (3) Assumptions and uncertainties: List every setup detail you are inferring because it is not stated in the available facts — include the exact metric definition, whether α is fixed vs layer-wise, whether KV is re-quantized each step, whether group-size quantization is in scope, eval prompt construction, and any codebase/resource assumptions. Flag anything that materially affects the design. Keep the response short; the full experiment design will be requested after approach review. Do not fabricate measurements or outcomes.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"How does the clipping ratio used during runtime quantization affect perplexity on LLAMA2-7B when applying symmetric input quantization and asymmetric KV cache quantization? What is the optimal fixed clipping ratio that balances quantization error and model accuracy in inference?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 24, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [\"neurips2024/94328/2:setup_1\", \"neurips2024/94328/2:setup_10\", \"neurips2024/94328/2:setup_17\"], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 1}
