en symmetric int): for token *t*, `m_t = max_i |x_{t,i}|` over the token's hidden vector; clipping ratio α ∈ (0, 1] defines `c_t = α · m_t`; then `q = round(x / s) · s`, `s = c_t / (2^(b-1) − 1)`, `b ∈ {4, 8}`. Out-of-range values are clipped. α is the swept variable.\n3. **KV-cache** (per-token, per-head-channel asymmetric uint): for each cached token's K and V, per head-channel axis compute `(min, max)` → store as `(scale, zero_point)`, bits ∈ {4, 8}. Re-quantized **every decode step from current FP activations** (newly produced K/V is asymmetric-quantized before being appended); previously stored KV entries remain in their already-quantized form and are dequantized on read.\n\n**Sweep axes (varied)**\n- α (clipping ratio for activations): 18 values, e.g. `{0.10, 0.20, …, 0.95, 1.00}` plus an orientation point at `α ≈ 0.693` derived from a per-tensor 3σ/percentile-99.9 rule (ASSUMPTION).\n- Weight bits × Activation bits ∈ `{W4A4, W4A8, W8A8}`.\n- KV bits ∈ `{K4V4, K4V8, K8V8}` (per cell).\n- With 3 (W,A) cells × 18 α × 3 KV configs ≈ **162 measured cells**, plus 1 FP16 baseline under matched eval conditions.\n\n**Held fixed**\n- Eval dataset, tokenizer, sequence length, sample count, KV quantization scheme, per-token/per-channel granularity, decoder (LM-loss only).\n\n**Evaluation metric — Perplexity**\n- PPL = `exp( mean( CE loss over all eval tokens ) )`. Report ΔPPL = PPL(α) − PPL(FP16) per cell.\n- Sliding-window PPL (stride = ctx) is a secondary check; primary = concatenated, non-overlapping PPL (ASSUMPTION).\n\n**Eval dataset (ASSUMPTION)**\n- WikiText-2 raw (`wikitext-2-raw-v1`), test split, concatenated, no chat template, BOS prepended, sliding windows over `seq_len`. Standard LLaMA perplexity convention.\n\n**Sequence length & sample count**\n- `seq_len = 2048` (LLaMA-2 default). Eval tokens ≈ 287 k (full WT-2 test); optional budget cap at first 256 k tokens (~125 windows) if compute is constrained.\n\n**Axes summary**\n| axis | values | role |\n|---|---|