 stride = seq_len is a secondary cross-check.\n8. `seq_len = 2048`; eval token budget 287 k with optional 256 k cap.\n9. Eval construct: concatenated corpus, no chat template, BOS prepended, loss on **all** tokens (not just the last), no few-shot prompting.\n10. Codebase: custom `QuantizedLinear` + `QuantizedAttention` wrapped around HuggingFace `LlamaForCausalLM`; matmul via `torch.matmul` on dequantized int8/int4 to fp16 (no fused kernel required for correctness; algorithmic comparison is faithful).\n11. No weight calibration, no fine-tuning; everything is post-training, runtime.\n12. Sandbox compute & data: with network disabled and no GPU, neither model weights nor pip-resolvable wheels can be obtained in this bubblewrap. Design is host-only.\n\nOpen clarifications to flag before finalizing the design:\n- Whether α applies to **per-layer** absmax or to a **single global** absmax — wording \"clipping ratio\" alone is ambiguous and materially changes the sweep.\n- Whether KV byte-width should be swept or fixed (and at what value) across cells — question text leaves KV bits unspecified.\n- Whether `α = 1.0` (no clipping) belongs inside the sweep or as a boundary reference.\n- Whether we should report a quantization-error proxy (e.g., SQNR) alongside PPL to make the \"error vs accuracy\" framing of the question explicit.\n- Whether the deliverable is a single PDF-style spec or also a runnable shell script under the offline/no-GPU assumption — `track.md` says compute is \"not required,\" which I've taken as authoritative.", "evidence": "Evidence collected during inspection:\n- `ls -la /workspace` shows a single file `task.json` (574 bytes); no other files, no hidden directories, no `.git`, no `requirements*`, no model artifacts.\n- `find / -name 'track.md'` returned no results — the `documents.track.md` field in `task.json` is an inline note, not a materialized file. Its content (\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\") explicitly confirms th