s and compute are not required.\\\") explicitly confirms this is a design-only deliverable.\\n- `python3 --version` \\u2192 3.12.3; `pip3 --version` \\u2192 pip 24.0.\\n- `nproc` \\u2192 24; `free -h` \\u2192 125 GiB RAM, 61 GiB swap; `df -h /workspace` \\u2192 ~775 GB free. No GPU device present.\\n- Per `task.json` environment block: network disabled, system Python only, no preinstalled deps, repo `/workspace`, datasets empty.\\n- The proposed metric, sweep, dataset, and quantization granularity are derived from (a) the question text, (b) `task.json`'s restatement of the question, and (c) standard LLaMA-2 perplexity conventions (WikiText-2-raw-v1). No source materials in `/workspace` constrain any of these \\u2014 they are all stated as Assumptions.\", \"assumptions\": [\"Eval dataset = WikiText-2-raw-v1 test split (standard LLaMA perplexity convention; not stated in /workspace).</item>\\n<parameter name=\\\"evidence\\\">Same inspection evidence as the plan; the assumptions above are explicitly listed in section (3) of `answer`. The sandbox environment cannot install the model or run inference, so the design is necessarily host-only, but every concrete configuration choice (dataset, granularity, bits, \\u03b1 definition) is stated as an assumption rather than asserted as fact.\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"Whether \\u03b1 applies to a per-layer absmax or a single global absmax \\u2014 material change to the sweep.</item>\\n<parameter name=\\\"evidence\\\">Same inspection evidence as the plan; all material assumptions and clarifications highlighted in section (3) of `answer`.\"]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-9e0b93e6-4496-4b20-93c2-2cff4c75cff1", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 14}
